  "summary": "A Virginia General Assembly bill (HB2724) would regulate use of automated license plate readers, including a 30-day retention cap. Charlottesville PD says its 10 Flock cameras already comply with stricter local policy (7-day retention, criminal-justice uses), while Albemarle County PD is relaunching mobile in-car ALPRs in five vehicles.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Automatic license plate readers are a tool of mass surveillance, so they capture not only the license plate as the name suggests, but the make and model of the vehicle as well",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "there are currently zero state laws regulating the use of ALPRs in Virginia",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Charlottesville only holds onto Flock data for seven days, which is well within the bill's proposed 30-day retention period",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
